# Solver run directories and the exports made from them: build artifacts,
# regenerated by `aicfd run` and `aicfd post` (ADR-004, ADR-032).
#
# The three WORKED results are evidence rather than artifacts -- the README,
# the ADRs and the experiment notes all cite them -- so they are tracked, under
# `reference/`, which the tool never writes to. A result you produce shadows
# the one shipped: the page looks in results/ first and falls back to
# reference/, so re-running a worked case can never collide with the copy in
# the repository.
runs/
results/

# Word reports and their figures: a deliverable, rebuilt from an export by
# `aicfd report` or the button on the results page. The document is the thing
# to hand someone, not the thing to version -- the export it was built from is.
reports/

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OpenFOAM artifacts, in case a case is ever solved in place
log.*
VTK/
processor*/
postProcessing/
**/constant/polyMesh/
*.foam
*.OpenFOAM

# Solver time directories (the 0/ initial conditions are versioned)
[1-9]/
[1-9][0-9]/
[1-9][0-9][0-9]/
[1-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/
[0-9]*.[0-9]*/
